        <div class="jcBand">
            <div id="pnlJobDescription">
	
                <h3 class="postingHeader">Job Description and Duties</h3>
                <p class="postingContent">
                    <div><span style="font-size: 12pt;">The California Lottery is looking for a highly experienced and seasoned Head of Promotions and Retail Marketing to develop, oversee, and lead the Lottery&#39;s retail marketing, promotions and event marketing efforts. </span></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><br />Under the general direction of the Chief of Consumer Marketing, the Head of Promotions and Retail Marketing (Staff Services Manager II) develops, manages, and oversees the Lottery&#39;s Promotions and Retail Marketing program. The Head of Promotions and Retail Marketing leads the team responsible for the development of Lottery’s retail marketing program and promotions to build the awareness of the Lottery brand, motivate users to play Lottery games, increase player loyalty to generate contributions to education. The Head of Promotions and Retail Marketing executes the strategic vision and drives the development and implementation of marketing programs designed to enhance the display, promotion, and awareness of Lottery products at Lottery retail locations. The Head of Promotions and Retail Marketing also leads the planning, development and execution of promotions and programs that assist the Sales team in maintaining, enhancing, and building trade relations with Lottery retailers, through promotions and targeted partnership programs. The Head of Promotions and Retail Marketing is also responsible for growing positive brand perception amongst California adults through live events, sponsorship, consumer promotions, product integrations and experiential efforts. The Head of Promotions and Retail Marketing ensures the unit’s programs and tactics follow approved strategies, delivers on objectives, and directs their team’s contributions to the annual marketing plan.</span></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><br />This position requires a current Staff Services Manager II exam. If you need to take the exam or if your score has expired, click&nbsp;</span><a href="https://calcareers.ca.gov/CalHrPublic/Exams/ExamBulletin.aspx?ExamControlId=2193" style="font-family: &quot;Microsoft Sans Serif&quot;; font-size: 11pt; text-decoration-line: none;"><span style="color: #467886; font-weight: bold; text-decoration-line: underline;">here</span></a>&nbsp;<span style="font-size: 12pt;">to gain list eligibility.</span></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><br />This position is headquartered in Sacramento and is eligible for a hybrid telework schedule. Employees must be able to report to their assigned headquarters office as assigned. Travel expense to and from the assigned headquarters are the responsibility of the employee. Eligibility for telework requires the employee to reside in California per California Government Code Section 14200 which states: “telecommuting means the partial or total substitution of computers or telecommunication technologies, or both, for the commute to work by employees residing in California.</span></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><br />When choosing a state organization to work for, there are a lot of options. Why choose the California State Lottery?  </span></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;"> <br /><strong>People are drawn to the Lottery because we:<br /> </strong></span></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;">•	Are an energetic, creative, and talented team</span></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;">•	Value diversity and inclusion in the workplace</span></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;">•	Empower team members to bring their knowledge, expertise, and innovation</span></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;">•	Recognize individual and team contributions</span></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;">•	Support the importance of work-life balance</span></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;">•	Invest in the professional development of our team members</span></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;">•	Are dedicated to preserving our environment by lowering our carbon footprint</span></div><span style="font-size: 12pt;"> </span><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><br /><strong>May consider a Training &amp; Development assignment.<br /> </strong></span></div><span style="font-size: 12pt;"> </span><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;">All Experience and Education relating to the Minimum Qualifications listed on the Classification Specification should be included to clearly demonstrate how you meet the Minimum Qualifications for the position on your State Application (STD Form 678). The application should also clearly demonstrate the candidate’s ability to meet the Desirable Qualifications identified in this job advertisement.  The Classification Specification is located on this Job Announcement Posting under &quot;Minimum Requirements.&quot;<br /><br /><span>New to State candidates are hired at the minimum salary of the classification.</span><br /><br /><strong>Applications will be reviewed on a daily basis.<br /> </strong> </span> </div><div><br /></div><div><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt 0pt 8pt; line-height: 1.07917;"><br /></p><span style="font-size: 12pt;"> </span></div><p>You will find additional information about the job in the <strong><a href='https://www.CalCareers.ca.gov/CalHrPublic/FileDownload.aspx?aid=26250976&name=DutyStatement.pdf' target='_blank'>Duty Statement</a></strong>.</p>
