    <div id="pnlDesirableQualifications" class="jcBand">
	
        <h3 class="postingHeader">Desirable Qualifications</h3>
        <div class="postingContent">
            In addition to evaluating each candidate's relative ability, as demonstrated by quality and breadth of experience, the following factors will provide the basis for competitively evaluating each candidate:
        </div>
        <div class="postingContent">
            <ul><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Bachelor&#39;s degree, preferably with a specialization in marketing, communications, business or related field.</span><span style="font-size: 12pt;"></span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">8+ years of experience in marketing at a managerial or senior staff level with an emphasis in one or more of these areas: retail marketing, events and experiential marketing, sponsorships, and/or consumer promotions.<br /></span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">4+ years of managerial experience and ability to lead a team. Must have the ability to provide direction, guidance, motivation and oversight to team members, in order to carry out plans and projects that meet objectives, time line and budget. Must also have strong team building skills to develop a collaborative performance culture. <br /></span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Excellent verbal/written communication skills and strong presentation skills.  Ability to communicate marketing strategies, plans and project updates and gain alignment with various stakeholders and leadership. Have the ability to weigh competing priorities, manage tradeoffs and evaluate opportunistic new ideas with leadership and stakeholders. <br /></span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Ability and experience in building successful relationships with internal and external stakeholders to establish collaborative partnerships and work as a collaborative member of the larger Marketing organization. <br /></span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Demonstrated experience in developing, implementing, and managing strategic marketing plans or efforts. Must have the ability to think strategically and tactically. <br /></span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Experience working with marketing and advertising agencies to manage strategic planning, creative development, production and timelines. Comfortable communicating with and giving direction to marketing agencies/vendors and creative staff.<br /></span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Marketing experience in the consumer packaged goods (CPG), entertainment, gaming or lottery industry preferred.<br /></span></li></ul>
        </div>
    
